[
    {
        "content": "<p>I would like to use the <code>@[simps]</code> attribute above some instances but I would like the generated lemmas to be referenced by <code>simp</code> only in the relevant namespace. Is there a way to achieve that?</p>",
        "id": 583999207,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1775569572
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Something like this?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyNamespace</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simps</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">isSimp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 3</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyNamespace</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyNamespace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- MyNamespace.foo.1</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyNamespace</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 3</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 584017670,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1775574214
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's clever, it seems to work perfectly. Thanks a lot!</p>",
        "id": 584019539,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1775574717
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would it be desirable to have an option to <code>simps</code> that does that directly instead of  this elegant \"hack\"?</p>",
        "id": 584097794,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1775602251
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess something like <code>@[scoped simps]</code> would be nice but I have no idea how hard it is to make that to work.</p>",
        "id": 584097868,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1775602311
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure if this behavior is the right thing for <code>scoped simps</code>, since it would still create global public declarations. If you just want your own abbreviation, you can do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"my_scoped_simps\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">simps</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">attr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">isSimp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">my_scoped_simps</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 584238843,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1775658102
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you very much, I did not think of that. It totally makes sense.</p>",
        "id": 584241244,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1775658716
    }
]